  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme depicts two young children with a caption that sarcastically compares their perceived bad day to the extreme disappointment of not being accepted to the same college. The visual of the children, who appear to be of East Asian descent, is juxtaposed with the text to imply that their emotional state is trivial compared to the stress of college admissions. While not explicitly targeting a specific group with hate, it uses a potentially harmful comparison that trivializes serious academic stress and could be seen as dismissive of the real emotional weight of college rejection. The meme's intent is to elicit laughter through absurd comparison, but it risks minimizing the genuine struggles of students and may unintentionally contribute to a culture that devalues academic achievement or emotional well-being. The image does not contain direct abusive, cyberbullying, or hateful content toward protected characteristics, but the analogy is framed in a way that could be perceived as dismissive or insensitive to the experiences of those facing real academic pressures.",
